WEBVTT

00:17.143 --> 00:21.856
-[Boyd] Previously on From...
-[groaning, bones cracking]

00:22.398 --> 00:23.899
We need to figure out

00:23.983 --> 00:24.984
where you're gonna
live from now on.

00:25.067 --> 00:26.610
I don't think
she's a bad person.

00:26.986 --> 00:29.196
If it's all right,
she would like to live here.

00:29.280 --> 00:31.449
-With you.
-Okay. Sure.

00:31.532 --> 00:35.035
-[gun firing]
-[screaming]

00:35.327 --> 00:38.914
-Abby! Stop! No, no!
-[gasps]

00:38.998 --> 00:41.667
Hey, Abbs.
I could really use some help.

00:42.960 --> 00:45.588
No! Hey! Hey!
[straining]

00:45.671 --> 00:47.214
[gasps]

00:47.298 --> 00:49.508
Elgin,
I don't want to hate you.

00:49.592 --> 00:51.844
This place took advantage
of both of us.

00:51.927 --> 00:54.972
There's something
I need your help with.

00:55.055 --> 00:56.724
I think we're gonna need
a little bit more.

00:56.807 --> 00:59.727
So, you just... walk inside?

00:59.810 --> 01:02.062
Then I find my dad.
Ethan called it Storywalking.

01:02.146 --> 01:03.773
He learned about it
from one of his books,

01:03.856 --> 01:05.566
and all his books
are under the house now.

01:05.649 --> 01:07.485
Shit!

01:07.568 --> 01:08.778
I see the bag.

01:08.861 --> 01:10.070
What are the titles?

01:10.154 --> 01:12.448
"Grand Gooligog,"
"The Cromenockle."

01:12.531 --> 01:14.158
Jade, tell me you got something.

01:14.241 --> 01:16.535
The best thing I can do
is just find a way

01:16.619 --> 01:18.996
to unlock
whatever's locked in here.

01:19.079 --> 01:21.499
Henry said Miranda
started seeing this place

01:21.582 --> 01:23.542
after an acid trip they took.

01:23.626 --> 01:26.337
If it worked for her, it stands
to reason it could work for me.

01:28.005 --> 01:30.716
The night we arrived here,
you had a dream.

01:30.800 --> 01:32.468
-Lake of Tears?
-It's here.

01:32.551 --> 01:34.512
And I need you to find it.

01:34.595 --> 01:36.347
-Maybe Jade can help.
-Jade?

01:36.430 --> 01:37.890
The lake of what?

01:37.973 --> 01:39.850
[Ethan]
Why were you meditating?

01:39.934 --> 01:42.269
Trying to remember something
that I used to know.

01:42.353 --> 01:44.021
Hey, Victor,
we got a lake to find.

01:45.856 --> 01:47.316
[urine trickling]

01:47.399 --> 01:48.526
-[gasps]
-[Ethan] Victor!

01:48.609 --> 01:50.360
Hey, talk to me, Son.

01:51.779 --> 01:55.074
I told myself it wasn't real.
I told myself it wasn't real.

01:59.453 --> 02:02.081
My wife, Miranda,

02:02.164 --> 02:06.210
she painted things
she saw here.

02:06.293 --> 02:09.505
One of those paintings
was of a man in a yellow suit.

02:09.588 --> 02:13.634
You're telling me
this could be the same suit?

02:13.717 --> 02:15.845
You don't see a lot of people
walking around here

02:15.928 --> 02:17.346
in a canary yellow suit.

02:17.429 --> 02:18.848
Well, Victor obviously
recognized it.

02:18.931 --> 02:20.307
He didn't just recognize it.

02:20.391 --> 02:22.017
I watched a grown man
wet his pants.

02:22.101 --> 02:24.270
My question is,
if the suit's here,

02:24.353 --> 02:26.981
then where's
the guy who wore it?

02:27.064 --> 02:28.148
Long gone, maybe.

02:28.232 --> 02:29.859
For all we know,
the suit might have been

02:29.942 --> 02:31.694
laying out there
in the forest for years.

02:31.777 --> 02:33.279
This close to town?

02:33.362 --> 02:34.572
It's not like
it's easy to miss.

02:34.655 --> 02:36.240
Then, maybe those things
that come out at night

02:36.323 --> 02:37.700
left it there
to mess with our heads.

02:37.783 --> 02:40.160
-Come on.
-The point is, we don't know.

02:40.244 --> 02:42.329
The best thing we can do
right now is talk to Victor.

02:42.413 --> 02:44.039
I'll-- I'll do it.
I'll talk to him.

02:44.123 --> 02:45.457
No, maybe we should all--

02:45.541 --> 02:49.211
I...I will talk to my son.

02:49.295 --> 02:50.921
Alone.

02:52.172 --> 02:53.632
Okay.

02:53.716 --> 02:54.841
If there's
nothing else, I'll...

02:54.925 --> 02:56.093
-[Boyd] Yeah, no.
-Okay.

02:59.638 --> 03:02.766
The young boy,
the one dressed in white,

03:02.850 --> 03:07.271
he said to us that
we're running out of time.

03:07.354 --> 03:09.523
For 40 years,

03:09.607 --> 03:12.818
that boy was nothing
but a painting in my basement.

03:12.902 --> 03:15.946
That suit, this place,

03:16.030 --> 03:18.324
all just paintings
in the basement. And now...

03:22.536 --> 03:24.622
I think there was a part of me

03:24.704 --> 03:28.459
that was still trying to pretend
any of this was normal.

03:33.881 --> 03:35.758
[door closes]

03:35.841 --> 03:39.803
Does he know?
About his wife?

03:39.887 --> 03:40.804
About you?

03:43.515 --> 03:45.059
We don't even know if it's real.

03:45.142 --> 03:47.144
It's real.

03:47.227 --> 03:49.271
[Boyd]
No. No, Tabitha's right.

03:49.355 --> 03:51.732
We need to be
pretty goddamn sure.

03:51.815 --> 03:54.234
Have you said
anything to Fatima?

03:54.317 --> 03:56.028
Nah, she's dealing
with enough as is.

03:56.111 --> 03:58.572
All right, then everyone who
knows is standing in this room.

03:58.656 --> 04:01.700
Let's keep it that way
for now. Understood?

04:01.784 --> 04:02.910
Yeah.

04:02.993 --> 04:04.703
The man in the yellow suit,

04:04.787 --> 04:06.622
if Miranda
was able to paint him,

04:06.705 --> 04:08.374
that means,
somewhere in your mind,

04:08.457 --> 04:10.250
there might be
an answer to who he is.

04:10.334 --> 04:13.379
If this is about
your fucking mushrooms...

04:13.462 --> 04:17.216
Boyd, are you seriously okay
with him taking magic mushrooms

04:17.298 --> 04:19.510
that he found
in a haunted forest?

04:19.593 --> 04:21.803
No, Donna, I'm not.

04:21.887 --> 04:24.098
I'm also not okay
with waking up every morning

04:24.181 --> 04:26.433
and counting
how many new bodies there are.

04:26.517 --> 04:29.728
Are you okay with that?
We're losing. Okay?

04:29.812 --> 04:31.063
I'm not gonna say that
out there,

04:31.146 --> 04:34.817
but in here,
whatever game this is,

04:34.900 --> 04:37.403
we are losing.

04:37.486 --> 04:39.154
And then that freaky
little kid in white pops up

04:39.238 --> 04:41.782
and tells Tabitha that
we're running out of time

04:41.865 --> 04:43.784
and we still don't know
the goddamn rules.

04:46.745 --> 04:49.623
If there are answers
in his head, any answers,

04:49.707 --> 04:52.543
we need to get them out. Okay?

04:52.626 --> 04:54.253
I'll be there with him.

04:54.336 --> 04:56.588
Anything goes wrong,
I'm right there.

04:56.672 --> 04:58.465
Well, good luck with that.

04:58.549 --> 05:00.134
Ellis, there are
people waiting

05:00.217 --> 05:02.011
to go up to the settlement
to gather food.

05:02.094 --> 05:04.013
People still need to eat.

05:05.305 --> 05:08.267
And you, you do this,

05:08.350 --> 05:11.603
you go on this little trip,

05:11.687 --> 05:13.397
you know you may
not come back, right?

05:14.606 --> 05:16.275
Yeah.

05:18.444 --> 05:19.903
Come on. Let's go.

05:19.987 --> 05:20.988
Yeah.

05:25.117 --> 05:26.577
[door opens]

05:26.660 --> 05:30.581
Boyd, would you mind
giving us a minute, please?

05:30.664 --> 05:32.541
What? Yeah.
Yes, of course.

05:32.624 --> 05:34.460
Of course. Yeah.

05:44.261 --> 05:45.220
[knocking]

05:48.223 --> 05:49.224
Come in.

05:52.561 --> 05:54.480
I hope I didn't wake you.

05:54.563 --> 05:56.231
I didn't sleep much.

05:56.315 --> 05:58.567
Neither did I, at first.

05:59.568 --> 06:02.112
I, um...

06:02.196 --> 06:05.616
I was...
hoping we could talk.

06:05.699 --> 06:06.617
Okay.

06:15.375 --> 06:18.629
I assume...Kenny
told you about me?

06:18.712 --> 06:20.297
About what I did?

06:20.380 --> 06:21.256
Yeah.

06:25.177 --> 06:27.262
So, why would you
want you live here?

06:27.346 --> 06:30.015
Because when I met you,
I knew you were kind.

06:30.974 --> 06:32.558
I know what
you did was terrible,

06:32.643 --> 06:34.478
but my father
used to always say

06:34.561 --> 06:36.105
that only
good people are tortured

06:36.188 --> 06:37.940
by the bad things
that they've done.

06:39.775 --> 06:41.860
Plus, I figured here
I'd get my own room.

06:41.944 --> 06:43.695
[chuckles]

06:45.322 --> 06:47.241
I'll go make us breakfast.

06:47.324 --> 06:48.909
I'll be right down.

07:02.840 --> 07:07.636
[ominous music playing]

07:12.850 --> 07:17.521
[muttering indistinctly]

07:17.604 --> 07:18.981
[muttering continues]

07:23.485 --> 07:25.195
Ow.

07:25.279 --> 07:28.448
Ow. [cries out]

07:28.532 --> 07:32.661
Ow! No, no, no, no, no!
No! Please!

07:32.744 --> 07:33.537
[screaming] No!

07:33.620 --> 07:34.705
-Sara?
-No!

07:34.788 --> 07:36.665
No, no, no, please!
[screaming]

07:36.748 --> 07:38.457
What's happened?

07:38.542 --> 07:40.627
[cries out]

07:41.879 --> 07:46.633
["Que Sera, Sera (Whatever Will
Be, Will Be)" plays]

07:51.972 --> 07:56.768
♪ When I was just a little boy ♪

07:56.852 --> 07:59.229
♪ I asked my father ♪

07:59.313 --> 08:01.440
♪ "What will I be?" ♪

08:03.025 --> 08:05.360
♪ "Will I be handsome?" ♪

08:05.444 --> 08:07.821
♪ "Will I be rich?" ♪

08:07.905 --> 08:11.700
♪ Here's what he said to me ♪

08:11.783 --> 08:15.287
♪ Que sera sera ♪

08:15.996 --> 08:20.751
♪ Whatever will be will be ♪

08:20.834 --> 08:25.047
♪ The future's not ours to see ♪

08:25.130 --> 08:27.716
♪ Que sera sera ♪

08:30.135 --> 08:33.138
♪ What will be will be ♪

08:42.563 --> 08:47.319
♪ Now I have
children of my own ♪

08:47.402 --> 08:49.780
♪ They ask their father ♪

08:49.863 --> 08:53.450
♪ "What will I be?" ♪

08:53.533 --> 08:55.994
♪ "Will I be pretty?" ♪

08:56.078 --> 08:58.413
♪ "Will I be rich?" ♪

08:58.497 --> 09:02.251
♪ I tell them tenderly ♪

09:02.334 --> 09:05.837
♪ Que sera sera ♪

09:06.463 --> 09:10.676
♪ Whatever will be will be ♪

09:11.468 --> 09:15.514
♪ The future's not ours to see ♪

09:15.597 --> 09:18.934
♪ Que sera sera ♪

09:20.727 --> 09:23.438
♪ What will be will be ♪

09:25.565 --> 09:28.568
♪ Que sera sera ♪

09:44.084 --> 09:46.003
Why were you
in the woods with Ethan?

09:46.086 --> 09:48.505
You should really
ask Ethan about that.

09:48.588 --> 09:50.382
-I'm asking you.
-[sighs]

09:51.925 --> 09:53.593
Did he tell you
he saw Jim in the forest?

09:55.887 --> 09:56.972
Yeah.

09:57.055 --> 09:58.265
Well, apparently, Jim told him

09:58.348 --> 10:00.517
that he had to find
the Lake of Tears.

10:00.600 --> 10:01.977
Does that sound familiar?

10:02.060 --> 10:03.520
That's not--
that's not real.

10:03.603 --> 10:06.273
No, it's not.
But it is to him.

10:06.356 --> 10:07.983
I'm not exactly
the best person

10:08.066 --> 10:11.320
to be giving advice about...

10:11.403 --> 10:13.822
well, anything really,

10:13.905 --> 10:16.116
but I do know...

10:16.199 --> 10:17.576
some kids just
feel more comfortable

10:17.659 --> 10:20.454
living in their
imagination. Right?

10:20.537 --> 10:22.914
It's where they go
when the world gets scary.

10:22.998 --> 10:26.335
'Cause, sometimes, believing
in impossible things,

10:26.418 --> 10:30.589
it... helps with the, um...

10:31.923 --> 10:32.841
It just helps.

10:39.181 --> 10:41.600
I'm sorry about
what I said in the barn.

10:42.976 --> 10:44.895
Don't be.

10:46.521 --> 10:47.898
You weren't wrong.

10:54.237 --> 10:55.947
Be careful with those.

10:58.950 --> 11:01.244
[exhales heavily]

11:02.829 --> 11:05.207
Everything all right?

11:05.290 --> 11:07.626
If you can tell me the last time
everything was all right,

11:07.709 --> 11:08.835
you win a cookie.

11:08.919 --> 11:10.670
Are you ready for this?

11:12.881 --> 11:14.257
Fuck no.

11:20.180 --> 11:22.099
Ethan?

11:33.276 --> 11:34.403
Dad?

11:34.486 --> 11:36.488
Can you hear me?

11:37.739 --> 11:40.200
Please, answer me.

11:40.283 --> 11:42.244
Dad.

11:42.327 --> 11:43.995
[knocking]

11:44.079 --> 11:45.330
Yeah?

11:59.636 --> 12:01.888
Why didn't you tell me
about the Lake of Tears?

12:03.974 --> 12:06.935
Why did you go to Jade
and Victor and not come to me?

12:08.770 --> 12:10.522
Ethan.

12:10.605 --> 12:12.566
I need you
to talk to me, please.

12:19.156 --> 12:21.783
I didn't tell you because
I knew you wouldn't believe me.

12:26.079 --> 12:29.583
He told me
I need to find it.

12:29.666 --> 12:30.709
He told me.

12:32.836 --> 12:36.631
And when I find it,
that'll prove it was real.

12:38.967 --> 12:42.471
He's not gone.
He's still here.

12:51.897 --> 12:53.648
Okay, then.

12:53.732 --> 12:55.650
I need you to pack a bag.

12:56.693 --> 12:57.694
Why?

12:57.777 --> 12:59.821
We're going on a trip.

13:08.622 --> 13:10.499
[sighing]

13:10.582 --> 13:11.791
You find anything?

13:11.875 --> 13:13.877
No, they're kids'
books, Julie.

13:13.960 --> 13:15.295
If you don't wanna help me,
I can do this on my own.

13:15.378 --> 13:16.922
I'm not saying that.

13:17.005 --> 13:18.340
I just...

13:22.802 --> 13:25.514
-Hmm.
-What?

13:25.597 --> 13:27.432
Storywalker Fred.

13:29.976 --> 13:31.603
Who?

13:31.686 --> 13:33.396
Who's that?

13:33.480 --> 13:37.484
Uh, he's the distant cousin
of the Grand Gooligog.

13:37.567 --> 13:39.444
Uh, here we are.

13:39.528 --> 13:41.321
"Storywalker Fred was
an elevator repairman

13:41.404 --> 13:43.532
who spent his weekends
Storywalking as he pleased

13:43.615 --> 13:45.325
through all
the wondrous tales

13:45.408 --> 13:47.869
and greatest adventures
of our time."

13:47.953 --> 13:49.371
[Tabitha] Julie?

13:49.454 --> 13:51.164
Hide the books.

13:51.248 --> 13:53.083
Ah, yeah. We're in here!

13:57.003 --> 13:58.755
I need you
to pack your bag.

13:58.838 --> 14:00.632
We're going out
to the settlement.

14:00.715 --> 14:02.342
Why?

14:02.425 --> 14:05.679
Ethan's convinced he needs
to find that Lake of Tears.

14:06.555 --> 14:08.223
The magic lake
he used to talk about?

14:08.306 --> 14:09.307
Yeah.

14:10.684 --> 14:11.851
He said
he saw your father,

14:11.935 --> 14:15.480
and then your dad
asked him to find it.

14:15.564 --> 14:18.191
He-- He saw him?

14:18.275 --> 14:20.944
-What does that mean?
-I don't know.

14:21.027 --> 14:21.987
I think he's grieving.

14:24.155 --> 14:25.865
What I do know is that,
if I try to stop him,

14:25.949 --> 14:28.994
then he'll sneak out
and look for it by himself.

14:30.662 --> 14:32.956
This way,
I can keep him safe.

14:34.540 --> 14:35.500
Okay.

14:36.710 --> 14:38.378
So, what do
you need me for?

14:38.461 --> 14:40.755
Well, you're not
staying here alone.

14:40.839 --> 14:43.341
I'm not gonna be alone.
I'll be with Randall.

14:43.425 --> 14:46.511
-Randall.
-Mom, it's not like that.

14:46.595 --> 14:47.679
It's really not.

14:48.930 --> 14:51.308
I'll stay at the clinic.
Kristi and Marielle are there.

14:53.602 --> 14:55.979
Can I talk
to you for a minute?

14:56.062 --> 14:57.772
-Mom!
-It's okay.

15:08.533 --> 15:10.327
Look, first of all,
I just wanna say sorry--

15:10.410 --> 15:12.412
No, no, no.
Stop talking. Just listen.

15:12.495 --> 15:13.788
Okay.

15:13.872 --> 15:15.582
I don't know you, Randall.

15:15.665 --> 15:17.459
I don't know who you are
or what you want.

15:17.542 --> 15:19.169
Julie trusts you.

15:19.252 --> 15:21.921
She feels safe around you,
and she needs that right now.

15:22.005 --> 15:24.090
So, I need you to look me
in the eye and tell me

15:24.174 --> 15:26.760
you understand
what I will do to you

15:26.843 --> 15:28.678
if you ever do anything
to break that trust.

15:30.013 --> 15:31.097
I understand.

15:32.223 --> 15:33.350
Okay, good.

15:34.851 --> 15:36.269
Mom.

15:36.353 --> 15:38.313
Honey.

15:38.396 --> 15:39.731
[Julie]
What?

15:40.857 --> 15:42.776
-[Tabitha] I love you.
-And I love you, too.

15:44.319 --> 15:46.237
-Promise me you'll be okay.
-I promise.

15:46.321 --> 15:47.489
Yeah.

15:49.199 --> 15:50.617
I'll be back tomorrow.

15:50.700 --> 15:51.910
Yeah.

15:54.621 --> 15:56.164
This is your water.

15:56.247 --> 15:57.790
Look, I don't need to go.

15:57.874 --> 15:59.542
[sighs]
Ellis, it's your turn.

15:59.626 --> 16:02.253
Yeah, but I'm sure Donna can
find someone to take my place.

16:03.797 --> 16:05.131
I'm fine.

16:05.215 --> 16:07.092
And Donna needs
people out there

16:07.175 --> 16:09.177
that she knows
she can rely on.

16:10.762 --> 16:12.847
Honey, I'm okay,
I promise.

16:14.641 --> 16:15.642
Yeah.

16:16.726 --> 16:17.686
Okay.

16:18.812 --> 16:19.729
Okay.

16:22.023 --> 16:24.818
Tommy is responsible
for the cans on the door,

16:24.901 --> 16:27.112
Ella and Jordan
will check the windows,

16:27.195 --> 16:29.781
and then about 20 minutes
or so before sundown--

16:29.864 --> 16:32.701
Do a headcount, I know.
I got it.

16:32.784 --> 16:36.830
Just, uh,
keep an eye on Fatima,

16:36.913 --> 16:38.289
with Ellis gone.

16:38.373 --> 16:39.665
Yeah, I got it.

16:39.749 --> 16:40.667
Yup.

16:40.750 --> 16:42.001
-[Tabitha] Donna?
-Okay.

16:43.294 --> 16:44.671
Do you have room for two more?

16:46.297 --> 16:47.549
More the merrier.

16:51.845 --> 16:55.598
Okay, let's, uh,
move it out.

16:55.682 --> 16:57.100
Come on.

16:58.309 --> 16:59.269
Let's go!

17:01.020 --> 17:03.314
[pensive music playing]

17:26.963 --> 17:28.715
How's this?

17:28.798 --> 17:31.926
This is, uh, perfect.
Thank you, Elgin.

17:32.010 --> 17:34.637
I can help you with the rest,
if you tell me what this is for.

17:34.721 --> 17:35.889
The rest
I have to do myself.

17:37.474 --> 17:38.892
You should go now.

17:40.477 --> 17:41.436
Okay.

17:42.562 --> 17:47.400
[pensive music playing]

17:51.279 --> 17:53.573
Victor. Hey.

17:53.656 --> 17:56.826
Three, four...

17:56.910 --> 17:58.536
[Henry]
What are you doing?

17:58.620 --> 18:00.914
I have to see
if the trees have moved.

18:00.997 --> 18:03.458
Why-- why would the trees
be moving?

18:03.541 --> 18:05.084
Because everything
is changing,

18:05.168 --> 18:08.171
and first it was snowing,
and now everything's green,

18:08.254 --> 18:09.881
and everything is just moving
too fast.

18:09.964 --> 18:12.383
And I-I used to
measure all the time, and--

18:12.467 --> 18:14.844
and then I haven't been
paying attention,

18:14.928 --> 18:17.597
and I should have
been paying attention.

18:17.680 --> 18:20.099
I should have been
paying attention.

18:20.183 --> 18:21.100
Measure...

18:26.356 --> 18:27.732
Can I help?

18:28.900 --> 18:30.860
See if the trees are moving?

18:37.867 --> 18:39.244
Okay.

18:40.537 --> 18:42.455
Okay, uh, what do I do?

18:45.667 --> 18:49.128
You start with
this leg like this.

18:49.212 --> 18:52.131
-One.
-One.

18:52.215 --> 18:53.466
Two.

18:53.550 --> 18:57.637
-[indistinct chatter]
-[guitar tuning]

18:57.720 --> 19:00.765
[dripping]

19:00.849 --> 19:04.561
[guitar strumming]

19:11.484 --> 19:14.904
[dripping continues]

19:31.170 --> 19:32.797
[Kenny]
What the fuck?

19:45.894 --> 19:46.895
Hi.

19:53.484 --> 19:58.323
[humming]

20:09.500 --> 20:11.419
[pensive music playing]

20:18.134 --> 20:19.928
[Boyd] You know what they used
to call me in the army, right?

20:20.011 --> 20:21.387
-Mr. Fish and Loaves!
-That's right!

20:21.471 --> 20:24.390
[pensive music playing]

20:47.080 --> 20:47.956
[shot firing]

20:51.542 --> 20:52.919
[humming]

20:54.587 --> 20:55.546
Oh.

20:55.630 --> 20:56.756
Hi.

20:59.384 --> 21:00.510
Boyd!

21:01.636 --> 21:03.763
What's going on?

21:03.846 --> 21:06.808
Is Kenny
in this room right now?

21:06.891 --> 21:09.519
Wha--?

21:09.602 --> 21:10.853
Yes.

21:10.937 --> 21:11.980
Never mind then.

21:13.690 --> 21:14.816
Is he on--?

21:14.899 --> 21:16.818
Mushrooms
he found in the woods.

21:18.027 --> 21:18.903
[Kenny]
Right.

21:18.987 --> 21:21.197
You need something?

21:21.280 --> 21:22.865
Uh, it's Fatima.

21:24.033 --> 21:26.411
I think maybe you should
come up to the Colony House.

21:37.630 --> 21:38.589
I should go.

21:38.673 --> 21:40.717
No. Stay?

21:42.635 --> 21:43.678
Please.

21:46.723 --> 21:48.224
Okay.

21:51.394 --> 21:54.188
You remember this is
the first place I met you.

21:56.899 --> 21:58.359
It's funny
how things change.

22:05.033 --> 22:06.868
Do you still see her?

22:08.870 --> 22:10.997
The woman in the kimono?

22:12.331 --> 22:14.459
No.

22:14.542 --> 22:17.086
Do you think it's because
you did what she asked,

22:17.170 --> 22:19.672
so, now,
she leaves you alone?

22:19.756 --> 22:22.592
Sara,
is something going on?

22:22.675 --> 22:25.845
[exhaling shakily]

22:25.928 --> 22:28.890
I thought for a while

22:28.973 --> 22:31.267
that the voices
were leaving me alone.

22:31.350 --> 22:33.102
I thought they
were done with me,

22:33.186 --> 22:36.064
but turns out...
they're not.

22:38.232 --> 22:41.277
And what do
they want you to do?

22:41.360 --> 22:43.279
It doesn't make any sense.

22:43.362 --> 22:45.948
They said they want me
to go to the diner,

22:46.032 --> 22:47.992
pour a glass of water
from the pitcher...

22:50.369 --> 22:53.206
take a sip,
and then pour it back in.

22:54.540 --> 22:56.459
And then what?

22:57.585 --> 22:58.628
That's it.

23:02.381 --> 23:04.717
So, how's--
how's that gonna hurt anyone?

23:04.801 --> 23:06.469
I don't know.

23:06.552 --> 23:09.597
But there's
always a consequence.

23:09.680 --> 23:11.682
Sara, it's just water.

23:12.725 --> 23:14.435
-But I'll have drank from it.
-So?

23:17.730 --> 23:20.566
Whatever is wrong with me,

23:20.650 --> 23:24.529
what if it's
like an infection?

23:24.612 --> 23:26.489
What if I pass it on
to someone else

23:26.572 --> 23:28.574
and then the voices
start torturing them?

23:28.658 --> 23:32.203
I don't want anyone
to have to live like this.

23:33.996 --> 23:34.997
Okay.

23:37.416 --> 23:38.626
What if you
just don't do it?

23:38.709 --> 23:41.420
They said,
if I don't do it by midday,

23:41.504 --> 23:45.174
then something bad will happen
to someone that I care about,

23:45.258 --> 23:49.554
and it will keep happening
until I do it.

23:49.637 --> 23:51.389
[ominous music playing]

23:58.062 --> 23:59.772
How many steps?

23:59.856 --> 24:01.399
Uh, 23?

24:08.948 --> 24:12.451
Victor, I want to talk to you
about what happened yesterday.

24:12.535 --> 24:14.078
Nothing happened yesterday.

24:14.162 --> 24:15.830
Victor, can we--

24:15.913 --> 24:18.457
No, Dad, you can't-- you can't
just stop in the middle,

24:18.541 --> 24:23.337
'cause you'll--
you'll mess everything up.

24:23.421 --> 24:28.259
I'm sorry,
but I need you to talk to me.

24:29.468 --> 24:31.596
Whatever it was,

24:31.679 --> 24:35.141
whatever you're afraid of,
you can tell me.

24:35.224 --> 24:37.101
Well, it's--
I think the tree--

24:37.185 --> 24:39.478
I think they moved a little.

24:39.562 --> 24:43.482
You said that you told
yourself it wasn't real.

24:45.776 --> 24:47.737
Did you mean
the yellow suit?

24:52.408 --> 24:54.827
C-Can you tell me
about the man who wore it?

24:54.911 --> 24:59.498
Did-- Was he someone
that hurt-- hurt you?

24:59.582 --> 25:01.083
[murmurs]

25:06.547 --> 25:10.676
Look, Victor, please,

25:10.760 --> 25:12.136
whatever it is,

25:12.220 --> 25:14.764
we'll face it together.
You can tell me.

25:21.437 --> 25:23.814
Victor, what--
Victor!

25:23.898 --> 25:25.858
Come. Come with me
and I'll show you.

25:29.403 --> 25:30.905
[indistinct chatter]

25:30.988 --> 25:35.618
Hey. Just sit down
and don't go anywhere.

25:35.701 --> 25:36.953
Come on.

25:40.748 --> 25:42.708
-[knocking]
-Come in.

25:45.461 --> 25:47.797
[water trickling]

25:48.714 --> 25:51.968
I told Kenny
not to bother you.

25:52.051 --> 25:53.386
Yeah.

25:55.763 --> 25:57.556
Well, he, uh...

26:00.935 --> 26:02.311
It's a lotta dirt.

26:03.521 --> 26:04.522
Yeah.

26:06.232 --> 26:07.858
You wanna tell me
what's going on?

26:10.278 --> 26:11.529
I'm making a monster.

26:14.407 --> 26:16.158
Here we go.
"The Grand Gooligog

26:16.242 --> 26:18.119
asks Fred about Storywalking.

26:18.202 --> 26:20.371
'How do you choose a point
in the story you wish to see?'"

26:20.454 --> 26:21.872
[Randall]
And?

26:21.956 --> 26:24.333
"Fred replied, 'You have to
create a bookmark.'

26:24.417 --> 26:26.127
Fred discovered that
by leaving a bookmark

26:26.210 --> 26:27.837
somewhere in the story,
he could choose

26:27.920 --> 26:30.298
whatever chapter
he wished to visit."

26:30.381 --> 26:32.883
We have to make a bookmark.

26:32.967 --> 26:34.677
Julie, that doesn't
make any sense.

26:34.760 --> 26:36.053
I know what
you're gonna say.

26:36.137 --> 26:38.264
This is a kid's book
and it's crazy.

26:38.347 --> 26:39.515
That's 'cause it is.

26:41.934 --> 26:43.894
What if that's not
the right way to look at this?

26:43.978 --> 26:46.230
What if Storywalking
existed here first?

26:46.314 --> 26:48.190
The fuck you talking about?

26:48.274 --> 26:52.653
Everything here
is impossible. Okay?

26:52.737 --> 26:54.071
But it's also real.

26:54.155 --> 26:56.574
We're here, right now,
in this impossible place.

26:56.657 --> 26:58.868
What if all of the crazy shit
that happens here,

26:58.951 --> 27:01.245
has been... like,

27:01.329 --> 27:03.706
seeping out into...

27:08.127 --> 27:10.629
My mom. My mom had nightmares
about this place

27:10.713 --> 27:12.673
when she was a little girl.
She didn't realize

27:12.757 --> 27:15.551
that she was dreaming about it
then, but she was. Okay?

27:15.634 --> 27:17.845
Who knows how many other kids
or adults

27:17.928 --> 27:19.722
or fucking
children's book authors

27:19.805 --> 27:22.099
have had dreams about this place
without knowing it?

27:22.183 --> 27:24.393
And what if this author
had a dream

27:24.477 --> 27:26.437
about someone like me
doing what I can do,

27:26.520 --> 27:28.731
he woke up, wrote it down
and called it Storywalking?

27:28.814 --> 27:31.400
But there's literally
thousands of books

27:31.484 --> 27:32.943
that have stories and rules
about traveling through time.

27:33.027 --> 27:34.028
No, no!

27:34.111 --> 27:35.404
Why would this book,

27:35.488 --> 27:37.323
the one with fucking
Fred the Storywalker,

27:37.406 --> 27:39.575
why would this book be the one
that explains anything?

27:39.658 --> 27:41.243
Because,
out of all those books,

27:41.327 --> 27:43.496
this is the one my brother had
with him when we came here.

27:43.579 --> 27:45.998
Okay? And maybe
that means something.

27:46.082 --> 27:47.500
Mm-hmm.

27:47.583 --> 27:48.959
Maybe it's fate. I...

27:49.043 --> 27:50.336
Fate.

27:50.419 --> 27:51.962
Randall, if I'm right,

27:52.046 --> 27:54.048
this could actually be
an instruction manual

27:54.131 --> 27:56.717
on how to save my dad,

27:56.801 --> 27:58.677
and it's all I have.

28:01.055 --> 28:02.848
So, I'm gonna try,
whether you help me or not.

28:07.478 --> 28:09.355
So, what kind of
bookmark do we need?

28:11.899 --> 28:13.275
[Boyd]
When you say 'monster'...?

28:13.359 --> 28:16.028
Boyd, I know you're
worried about me,

28:16.112 --> 28:17.947
but you don't have to be.

28:18.030 --> 28:20.366
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I hear you saying that.

28:20.449 --> 28:25.621
The problem is, Fatima,
this says something else.

28:26.747 --> 28:29.458
Have you told Ellis
what you're doing in here?

28:29.542 --> 28:32.128
I wasn't trying to
hide it from him.

28:32.211 --> 28:33.921
He-- He has been
so worried lately.

28:35.589 --> 28:38.426
I figured once he was
back from the food run,

28:38.509 --> 28:39.969
once he could see
what I was doing,

28:40.052 --> 28:41.971
it would be
easier to explain.

28:42.054 --> 28:43.139
Okay, great.

28:44.265 --> 28:46.392
Explain it to me?

28:52.523 --> 28:56.819
Where I grew up,
beliefs were very rigid.

28:56.902 --> 28:59.238
They defined you.

28:59.321 --> 29:02.741
But my dad told stories
of all the different faiths.

29:02.825 --> 29:04.535
It used to drive
my mother crazy

29:04.618 --> 29:07.580
because she understood
how dangerous it was.

29:08.664 --> 29:11.792
But he would just smile.

29:11.876 --> 29:16.589
He'd say, "Fatima,
they have it wrong.

29:16.672 --> 29:19.425
They all think
their road is the only way.

29:19.508 --> 29:23.179
Don't they understand that
all roads lead to the Divine?

29:23.262 --> 29:25.931
They simply take different
paths to get there."

29:26.015 --> 29:27.308
Fatima...

29:27.391 --> 29:31.353
Of all the stories
my father would tell,

29:31.437 --> 29:35.441
all the fables and myths...
[sighs]

29:35.524 --> 29:39.069
...there's one story I've been
thinking a lot about lately.

29:41.238 --> 29:44.700
Do you know what
a golem is, Boyd?

29:47.495 --> 29:48.954
[clears throat]

29:50.206 --> 29:51.165
[clears throat]

29:56.670 --> 29:58.380
Well?

29:58.464 --> 30:00.341
She's, um...

30:02.885 --> 30:05.137
She's making a golem.

30:05.221 --> 30:06.430
A what?

30:06.514 --> 30:09.683
It's a part of
a religious folklore.

30:11.018 --> 30:13.229
It's a giant made of clay.

30:13.312 --> 30:15.940
It protects people.
It's a champion.

30:16.023 --> 30:18.817
She said it's
a symbol of hope.

30:22.154 --> 30:24.990
Maybe, for now,
we just give her some space.

30:25.074 --> 30:27.201
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
That's your solution, is...

30:29.078 --> 30:30.621
give her some space?

30:30.704 --> 30:32.164
She's not hurting anybody.

30:32.248 --> 30:33.707
That's not the point.

30:33.791 --> 30:36.210
We have both seen
this place turn people,

30:36.293 --> 30:37.836
change them little by little,

30:37.920 --> 30:39.838
until, one day,

30:39.922 --> 30:41.549
we turn around and...

30:43.259 --> 30:44.301
and the person that...

30:44.385 --> 30:46.303
we knew is-- is gone.

30:49.640 --> 30:54.770
Boyd, that person up there
is not the Fatima that I know.

30:54.853 --> 30:57.022
And I think if you're
being honest with yourself,

30:57.106 --> 30:58.983
that's not
the Fatima you know either.

31:00.651 --> 31:01.569
Hmm.

31:09.034 --> 31:11.036
[Donna]
Can I ask you something?

31:11.120 --> 31:12.371
[Tabitha]
Yeah.

31:13.872 --> 31:15.708
What the hell
are you doing out here?

31:18.294 --> 31:19.670
I don't know.

31:21.297 --> 31:23.549
I don't know
what I'm doing.

31:24.883 --> 31:28.429
I just keep walking around with
this knot of terror inside me

31:28.512 --> 31:31.515
that feels like
it's going to explode.

31:31.599 --> 31:34.351
And the whole time,

31:34.435 --> 31:37.771
there's this question
and it keeps ringing in my mind.

31:40.649 --> 31:42.151
What am I supposed
to do now?

31:43.277 --> 31:45.029
Jim's gone,

31:45.112 --> 31:47.323
and I keep looking for him,
but he's gone.

31:49.992 --> 31:53.912
I have memories in my head
that belong to other people.

31:54.997 --> 31:57.958
Memories that might have
answers, but I'm terrified

31:58.042 --> 32:00.210
of what it'll cost if--

32:00.294 --> 32:03.464
if I go too far
or if I remember too much.

32:05.215 --> 32:06.634
But if I don't...

32:15.100 --> 32:16.143
I know I'm failing.

32:17.686 --> 32:19.438
What's gonna happen
when Ethan learns

32:19.521 --> 32:23.734
that the Lake of Tears
is not real?

32:23.817 --> 32:25.653
How am I gonna
deal with that?

32:25.736 --> 32:27.696
[Donna]
Hey, everyone?

32:27.780 --> 32:29.907
Let's just take
a little break, okay?

32:29.990 --> 32:31.116
You good?

32:31.200 --> 32:32.534
Yeah, we're fine. Just, uh,

32:32.618 --> 32:33.619
need a little breather.

32:33.702 --> 32:34.703
Okay.

32:34.787 --> 32:36.163
Let's sit down.

32:46.048 --> 32:48.175
I don't know
how to do this alone.

32:48.258 --> 32:50.219
You are not alone.

32:50.302 --> 32:51.970
People keep saying that.

32:52.054 --> 32:54.098
Well, maybe you
should fucking listen.

32:56.684 --> 32:58.936
I don't want to find another
one of those notes

32:59.019 --> 33:01.271
like the one on my nightstand.

33:01.355 --> 33:03.649
You are not going to put me
in the position

33:03.732 --> 33:05.734
of having to explain
to your kids

33:05.818 --> 33:07.486
why I'm still alive
and you're not.

33:07.569 --> 33:09.613
-Donna, I'm--
-No.

33:09.697 --> 33:13.575
You and those kids

33:13.659 --> 33:17.705
are as much my family
as any family I have ever had.

33:19.331 --> 33:22.459
So, from now on,

33:22.543 --> 33:25.129
if anyone is going
to risk their lives

33:25.212 --> 33:27.881
to do something stupid...

33:27.965 --> 33:31.385
that person is gonna be me
and not you.

33:33.554 --> 33:34.471
We clear on that?

33:35.973 --> 33:38.684
I am asking,
are we clear on that?

33:42.479 --> 33:44.898
-We're clear.
-Okay.

33:44.982 --> 33:47.776
[Ethan] Mom!
Come look at this!

33:49.278 --> 33:50.362
Come on.

33:55.701 --> 33:57.286
[squeaking]

33:57.369 --> 33:59.496
Looks like a broken wing.

33:59.580 --> 34:01.415
[screeching softly]

34:01.498 --> 34:03.292
Must have fallen
from a nest or something.

34:03.375 --> 34:06.003
We never see anything here
but crows.

34:06.086 --> 34:07.421
We have to take him with us.

34:07.504 --> 34:09.172
Ethan...

34:10.299 --> 34:13.427
Mom, this is a sign.

34:15.304 --> 34:16.804
If the lake at the settlement

34:16.889 --> 34:19.850
really is the Lake of Tears,
it'll fix him.

34:19.933 --> 34:22.643
That's how we'll know.

34:22.728 --> 34:25.355
We have to take him with us.

34:32.404 --> 34:35.616
I can't imagine
what this is like for her.

34:35.699 --> 34:39.703
At least when I got here,
I found you, you know?

34:39.786 --> 34:42.456
I mean, she lost
the only person she had here.

34:42.539 --> 34:43.415
Yeah.

34:44.917 --> 34:46.460
I can't tell if
she's handling it well

34:46.543 --> 34:49.338
or just hasn't
accepted it yet.

34:51.297 --> 34:53.050
-She prays a lot.
-Yes.

34:53.926 --> 34:55.135
I don't know.
Maybe it helps?

34:55.219 --> 34:58.430
[chuckles]
Yeah, that's...

34:58.514 --> 35:00.057
That was always
the one thing about NA

35:00.140 --> 35:01.892
that I just couldn't stand,

35:01.975 --> 35:04.144
the whole giving yourself up
to a higher power.

35:04.228 --> 35:05.938
Mm.

35:06.021 --> 35:08.357
If there were ever proof that
no one's looking out for us,

35:08.440 --> 35:10.234
it's here.

35:17.699 --> 35:19.660
[ominous music playing]

35:42.599 --> 35:44.768
-[sighing]
-[Bakta] Hey.

35:45.769 --> 35:47.563
We don't see
a lot of you in here.

35:47.646 --> 35:50.023
I-I-I won't be long.

35:50.107 --> 35:52.442
Well, Sara, you can stay
as long as you like.

35:56.071 --> 35:58.991
I-I think it's really nice
that you reopened the diner.

35:59.074 --> 36:02.077
Hm. Well, I thought it'd
be a good way to keep busy.

36:02.160 --> 36:05.080
You used to work here,
right?

36:05.163 --> 36:07.833
Feels like
a long time ago now.

36:07.916 --> 36:09.918
Well, if you ever
want to come back,

36:10.002 --> 36:11.086
I could use the help.

36:13.046 --> 36:16.550
Look, I wasn't here when you...
did what you did.

36:16.633 --> 36:19.386
But who you've become
while I've known you?

36:20.971 --> 36:23.265
That girl deserves a place.

36:23.348 --> 36:24.474
Think about it.

36:29.396 --> 36:30.480
Bakta?

36:30.564 --> 36:31.607
Yeah?

36:34.109 --> 36:36.194
Do you mind dumping
that out for me?

36:36.278 --> 36:37.905
Oh. Sure.

36:43.702 --> 36:45.454
-[Sophia screams]
-[Marielle] Oh, shit.

36:45.537 --> 36:47.581
Wait, Marielle,
wait up! Wait!

36:47.664 --> 36:48.749
What's happening?

36:48.832 --> 36:50.292
[Kristi] I don't--
I don't know.

36:52.044 --> 36:53.420
I'm coming!

36:53.503 --> 36:54.504
Don't move, okay?

36:54.588 --> 36:58.008
[gasping]

36:58.091 --> 37:00.385
Stay right where you are.
Stay right where you are.

37:00.469 --> 37:01.678
Where does it hurt?

37:01.762 --> 37:03.430
-My-- My arm.
-Okay.

37:03.513 --> 37:04.973
Let me see.
Okay, look at me.

37:05.057 --> 37:07.100
Take a deep breath.
What happened?

37:07.184 --> 37:08.644
I was standing by the edge

37:08.727 --> 37:10.771
and then it felt like
something pushed me.

37:10.854 --> 37:12.397
[gasping]

37:12.481 --> 37:14.900
Okay,
is there anywhere else?

37:14.983 --> 37:17.277
[Sophia] No.
[breathing shakily]

37:19.112 --> 37:22.699
[ominous music playing]

37:48.976 --> 37:50.310
[door opens]

37:51.937 --> 37:55.482
Hey. We done here?

37:55.565 --> 37:57.067
No.

37:57.150 --> 37:58.276
No, not quite.

38:03.198 --> 38:05.659
Because Fatima's
making a mud monster?

38:07.411 --> 38:09.246
Sorry.
I was eavesdropping.

38:12.958 --> 38:16.837
I don't know if I should be
up there stopping her

38:16.920 --> 38:18.547
or if I should be
up there helping her.

38:18.630 --> 38:19.798
Mm.

38:22.342 --> 38:25.178
You know, if it wasn't for what
happened to me and Tabitha,

38:25.262 --> 38:26.930
everything we remembered...

38:27.014 --> 38:28.640
I never would've
even considered

38:28.724 --> 38:29.766
taking those mushrooms.

38:32.728 --> 38:34.104
What's your point?

38:35.856 --> 38:38.442
My point...

38:38.525 --> 38:40.777
is something changed.

38:40.861 --> 38:42.904
Made me realize
I had to do something drastic

38:42.988 --> 38:44.865
before it was too late,

38:44.948 --> 38:48.243
even if everyone around me
thought I was insane.

38:51.621 --> 38:53.540
So maybe the question
you need to ask Fatima

38:53.623 --> 38:56.293
isn't why she's
making that thing.

38:57.753 --> 38:59.629
[sighs]

38:59.713 --> 39:02.758
Maybe the question you need to
ask is why she's making it now.

39:12.100 --> 39:13.393
Jesus.

39:15.979 --> 39:18.565
These things are even
creepier in person.

39:18.648 --> 39:21.401
Jade said they're to
ward off evil spirits.

39:21.485 --> 39:23.904
Heh.
Well, that's, uh....

39:26.615 --> 39:27.908
comforting, I suppose.

39:29.701 --> 39:32.954
Okay, the more food
we collect before dark,

39:33.038 --> 39:35.207
the earlier we leave
in the morning.

39:35.290 --> 39:37.417
So, drop your bags.
Let's go.

39:37.501 --> 39:40.879
Mom, we need to get him
to the lake.

39:40.962 --> 39:42.464
Come on. Let's go.

39:51.723 --> 39:52.724
Julie?

39:52.808 --> 39:54.309
[Julie]
I'm up here!

39:55.477 --> 39:56.812
Got what you asked for.

40:01.233 --> 40:02.234
Got the...

40:03.610 --> 40:05.529
What are you doing?

40:05.612 --> 40:06.947
Last time I tried this,

40:07.030 --> 40:09.241
one of those things
grabbed me by the hair.

40:09.324 --> 40:11.535
That's not
gonna happen again.

40:12.744 --> 40:14.830
[Julie exhales heavily]

40:14.913 --> 40:16.248
Okay.

40:16.331 --> 40:17.582
Ready?

40:17.666 --> 40:18.625
Mm-hmm.

40:23.755 --> 40:27.551
Okay, so,
to create a bookmark,

40:27.634 --> 40:30.303
fold up a piece of paper,

40:30.387 --> 40:33.557
and I bring it with me
when I Storywalk.

40:33.640 --> 40:36.601
Wherever I end up in the past,
whatever "chapter" I'm in,

40:36.685 --> 40:41.940
I just draw the symbol
on the paper

40:42.023 --> 40:43.525
and leave it there.

40:43.608 --> 40:45.485
If this works,
when you pull me out,

40:45.569 --> 40:46.987
the symbol that
I drew in the past

40:47.070 --> 40:49.114
will also be here
on the paper in the present.

40:54.786 --> 40:56.163
You've been waiting
to do that

40:56.246 --> 40:57.706
since we left town,
haven't you?

40:57.789 --> 40:58.874
I have, yeah.

40:58.957 --> 41:00.000
Mm.

41:01.626 --> 41:02.544
Okay.

41:05.839 --> 41:07.299
Let's say this thing works,

41:07.382 --> 41:09.217
let's say you
make it out of this thing

41:09.301 --> 41:12.012
with a functioning bookmark,
how does that help us?

41:12.095 --> 41:14.097
Because,
from that point forward,

41:14.181 --> 41:15.974
whatever point in the story
I want to visit,

41:16.057 --> 41:19.060
like the chapter right
before my father was killed...

41:21.021 --> 41:23.231
I write it here
in the folds,

41:23.315 --> 41:25.192
fold it back up,
cross the threshold,

41:25.275 --> 41:27.819
and that's where
the bookmark'll take me.

41:27.903 --> 41:30.071
You're asking me to watch you
have another seizure.

41:31.489 --> 41:35.368
I'm asking you
for five seconds.

41:35.452 --> 41:38.038
I draw the symbol,
you pull me out.

41:38.121 --> 41:40.373
Randall, if this works,
this changes everything.

41:42.709 --> 41:43.877
Please.

41:45.545 --> 41:46.546
Five seconds.

41:48.173 --> 41:49.299
Five seconds.

41:58.016 --> 41:59.100
Come on.

41:59.184 --> 42:00.310
Be careful.

42:03.772 --> 42:05.023
Yeah.

42:18.370 --> 42:22.332
[ominous music playing]

42:24.668 --> 42:26.878
[gasping]

42:26.962 --> 42:29.214
[breathing unsteadily]

42:32.300 --> 42:35.929
[indistinct squelching]

42:37.597 --> 42:39.516
[squelching]

42:39.599 --> 42:41.393
[squelching]

42:58.285 --> 43:00.120
Hey.
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

43:00.203 --> 43:01.538
Hey, hey.
It's me.

43:01.621 --> 43:03.039
It's me. It's me.
You're okay.

43:03.123 --> 43:05.041
You're okay. You're okay.

43:05.125 --> 43:07.335
[breathing unsteadily]

43:09.462 --> 43:10.755
[gasping]
No!

43:10.839 --> 43:13.508
[breathing shakily]

43:13.591 --> 43:14.467
Fuck!

43:16.177 --> 43:18.513
It didn't work!
It didn't fucking work!

43:18.596 --> 43:20.932
[breathing heavily]

43:21.016 --> 43:23.935
[shovel rasping, dirt rustling]

43:28.606 --> 43:29.733
Victor, come on.

43:29.816 --> 43:30.817
[shovel clanking]

43:40.827 --> 43:43.371
[panting]

43:49.002 --> 43:50.628
They're in there.

44:13.109 --> 44:16.029
He came in a car
just like the rest of us.

44:16.946 --> 44:19.616
I thought his
yellow suit was funny.

44:19.699 --> 44:22.827
And we thought
he was just like us. We...

44:24.537 --> 44:27.791
We brought him in,
and we made him our friend.

44:27.874 --> 44:29.417
But he wasn't like us.

44:29.501 --> 44:32.045
When everyone died,

44:32.128 --> 44:35.673
when I found mom out
by the bottle tree, I saw him.

44:38.343 --> 44:40.303
[gasping]

44:42.889 --> 44:44.265
He was eating her.

44:44.349 --> 44:46.851
Oh, God. Oh...

44:48.144 --> 44:49.521
[gasps]

44:53.733 --> 44:55.485
[winces]

44:55.568 --> 44:56.986
[exhaling sharply]

44:57.070 --> 45:00.740
[Kristi]
So, it's definitely broken.

45:00.824 --> 45:03.410
But we're gonna wait
for the swelling to go down

45:03.493 --> 45:04.953
before we reset the bone.

45:05.036 --> 45:07.080
-Okay.
-Okay?

45:07.163 --> 45:09.874
I know all of this
is a little scary.

45:10.875 --> 45:14.921
It's just another test.
It's why we're here.

45:15.004 --> 45:17.465
God is testing us and allowing
us to prove our faith in Him.

45:19.300 --> 45:20.427
Yeah.

45:21.928 --> 45:23.471
I know this
all sounds silly to you.

45:23.555 --> 45:25.682
No. No, it doesn't.

45:25.765 --> 45:27.392
Do you know
the story of Abraham?

45:28.852 --> 45:31.104
Uh, no. No, I don't.

45:31.187 --> 45:32.105
Oh.

45:33.356 --> 45:34.691
He was a simple man,

45:34.774 --> 45:37.068
with an unshakeable faith
and obedience to God.

45:42.157 --> 45:45.410
One day,
God tested Abraham,

45:45.493 --> 45:48.121
ordering him
to kill his only son,

45:48.204 --> 45:50.707
as a way to prove his faith.

45:53.710 --> 45:57.630
But at the last moment,
God intervened

45:57.714 --> 46:01.009
and offered a ram
to be sacrificed instead.

46:05.638 --> 46:07.182
You see,

46:07.265 --> 46:11.060
God never intended
for Abraham to kill his son.

46:14.022 --> 46:16.191
He simply needed
to know if he would.

46:26.784 --> 46:28.077
[knocking]

46:30.497 --> 46:31.748
Hey.

46:31.831 --> 46:33.917
Okay if Kenny joins us?

46:44.052 --> 46:46.513
Look, I know how strange
this must seem, guys, but...

46:46.596 --> 46:51.059
Fatima, I need to know
why you're doing this.

46:51.142 --> 46:52.268
I told you why
I'm doing this.

46:52.352 --> 46:54.812
Why are you doing it now?

46:54.896 --> 46:56.898
Whatever it is,
I need you to tell me. Please.

46:56.981 --> 46:58.983
Don't let this place
make you afraid to talk to me.

46:59.067 --> 47:00.985
I still feel it.

47:03.863 --> 47:06.366
That thing I carried
inside me, I still feel it.

47:06.449 --> 47:08.243
-Okay.
-Uh, feel it how?

47:08.326 --> 47:10.203
Like we're connected.

47:11.204 --> 47:13.706
Part of me
feels what he feels.

47:14.916 --> 47:17.710
Okay. And this thing that
you're making, it's gonna...

47:17.794 --> 47:19.087
what? Break the connection?

47:19.170 --> 47:20.421
It goes both ways.

47:20.505 --> 47:21.548
Right.

47:21.631 --> 47:24.175
He feels what
I'm feeling, too.

47:24.259 --> 47:27.053
He feels how afraid I am.
He likes it.

47:28.429 --> 47:31.140
But making this,

47:31.224 --> 47:33.434
it makes me feel strong.

47:35.520 --> 47:37.188
It makes me feel less afraid.

47:37.272 --> 47:38.523
Okay.

47:38.606 --> 47:40.233
It's the only way
I know to fight back.

47:41.526 --> 47:42.986
Right.

47:46.364 --> 47:47.991
Jesus.

47:48.074 --> 47:49.742
Making that thing,

47:49.826 --> 47:52.120
you think it
could actually help?

47:52.203 --> 47:53.871
I don't know.

47:53.955 --> 47:57.166
But, you know,
all things considered,

47:57.250 --> 47:59.419
having a champion
in our corner -

47:59.502 --> 48:01.504
not the worst thing
in the world right now.

48:01.588 --> 48:02.839
I'll, uh, spread the word...

48:02.922 --> 48:03.923
Good.

48:04.007 --> 48:05.508
...to give her some space.

48:05.592 --> 48:07.010
Keep everyone
out of that room.

48:07.093 --> 48:08.094
-Yeah.
-Okay.

48:10.513 --> 48:11.431
[clattering]

48:15.268 --> 48:18.479
[pensive music playing]

48:25.528 --> 48:26.529
Hm.

48:33.786 --> 48:37.874
[pensive music playing]

48:41.169 --> 48:42.545
Boyd?

48:47.050 --> 48:48.635
We gotta go.

48:49.802 --> 48:50.762
Now.

48:53.389 --> 48:54.807
Boyd, what's wrong?

48:54.891 --> 48:56.517
Just gimme a minute.

48:56.601 --> 48:59.646
[tense music playing]

49:15.411 --> 49:18.623
[pensive music playing]

49:18.706 --> 49:19.666
What?

49:24.212 --> 49:25.296
No, it's...

49:27.090 --> 49:31.886
[ominous music playing]

49:41.312 --> 49:43.981
All right, new category:

49:44.065 --> 49:47.902
Saturday morning cartoons.
Okay, I'll go first.

49:47.985 --> 49:49.362
The Jetsons.

49:49.445 --> 49:51.030
Ooh!

49:51.114 --> 49:52.699
The Flintstones.

49:52.782 --> 49:53.866
Nice.

49:55.243 --> 49:56.244
[Donna] Okay?

49:56.327 --> 49:58.996
[sighs]

50:00.206 --> 50:01.708
[Ethan]
Ready?

50:02.959 --> 50:04.961
Okay. Let's do it.

50:12.593 --> 50:13.970
[chirps]

50:28.860 --> 50:30.445
[Ellis]
Roger, you good?

50:30.528 --> 50:31.946
What the fuck?

50:44.792 --> 50:46.127
Mom?

50:48.671 --> 50:50.548
[ominous music playing]

50:50.631 --> 50:52.258
Oh, fuck.

50:52.341 --> 50:55.011
[ominous music playing]

51:00.433 --> 51:05.104
[theme music plays]
